{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2292 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "de725007ff22136acf74ac69d61844490ad7fbc0e84bad86d3acf8ed7aa19741" :edb/db-before-t 2291 :edb/db-after-t 2292 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535604 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:23:45.804Z" 13194139535604 true] [17592186157239 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357190 13194139535604 true] [17592186157239 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357195 13194139535604 true] [17592186157239 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357202 13194139535604 true] [17592186310391 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041015/assets/e5c7f025b6f12599a4ecb5fa0cc9e657fd0b67deb1e50231673113f337ca7776.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139535604 false] [17592186310391 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068270/assets/e5c7f025b6f12599a4ecb5fa0cc9e657fd0b67deb1e50231673113f337ca7776.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139535604 true] [17592186310419 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041015/assets/7cb71517fe60c9d15b6cacddbf5f91c2e4a60103b8917a4d9baa287517a5fd54.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139535604 false] [17592186310419 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068270/assets/7cb71517fe60c9d15b6cacddbf5f91c2e4a60103b8917a4d9baa287517a5fd54.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139535604 true] [17592186357190 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357191 13194139535604 true] [17592186357190 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357193 13194139535604 true] [17592186357190 1089 "q-323209" 13194139535604 true] [17592186357190 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535604 true] [17592186357190 1100 "Consider the following parametric equation of the parabola\n\n$$\nx+7=-3t,\\,y-2=-9{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this parabola is\n\n$(x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139535604 true] [17592186357190 1113 #uuid "f54dfea7-1ce0-53bf-b599-41fdc4b47216" 13194139535604 true] [17592186357190 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-\\frac{x+7}{3},\\,{t}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{9}(y-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{x+7}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+7)^{2}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{9}(y-2)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+7)^{2}}{9} & =-\\frac{1}{9}(y-2) \\\\ {(x+7)}^{2} & =-(y-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535604 true] [17592186357191 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357192 13194139535604 true] [17592186357191 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535604 true] [17592186357191 1041 "field-1" 13194139535604 true] [17592186357191 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357192 13194139535604 true] [17592186357191 1110 #uuid "767456eb-e8d8-5700-beb7-2079e41ff6b7" 13194139535604 true] [17592186357192 1034 "7" 13194139535604 true] [17592186357192 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535604 true] [17592186357192 1111 #uuid "f0ce42e4-a7d5-57da-b3dd-eb27f70938d6" 13194139535604 true] [17592186357193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357194 13194139535604 true] [17592186357193 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535604 true] [17592186357193 1041 "field-2" 13194139535604 true] [17592186357193 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357194 13194139535604 true] [17592186357193 1110 #uuid "73ea54b2-2395-5bdf-9780-650ffe